  "pass_a_gloss": "The irrational impulses of the fathers are called 'sheep' and 'calves,' not because all such impulses are praiseworthy, but some are blameworthy like the sheep of sinful fathers, while others are praiseworthy, as when Christ says 'My sheep hear my voice,' and we, having the good shepherd in our souls, must have Christ dwelling within us as the good shepherd who governs our inner irrational motions so they do not wander aimlessly but are brought under his control, making what was once alien his own, so that when the shepherd is within us, he rules our senses, and nothing remains alien to the mind or under Pharaoh or Nebuchadnezzar, but all is under the good shepherd.",
